# GUI margins and spacing (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08): **margins and spacing keep getting
violated by default.** Empty top dead zones and cramped header-to-control
gaps ship in configurators and operator shells. This rule binds agent
UI-generation behavior for **every** operator GUI in the workspace.

## The rule

> **Professional, consistent margins and control spacing. Never ship
> large empty non-functional whitespace (especially large top dead
> zones). Never ship cramped controls against headers or window edges.**

Applies to **all** operator GUIs:

| Surface | Scope |
| --- | --- |
| Win32 dialogs | Client / server configurators, elevate helpers, product launchers |
| Tauri shells | Same product family — CSS / theme spacing, not ad-hoc spacer stacks |
| Admin SPA | Layout chrome (page padding, section headers vs fields) where this rule applies; DataGrid density remains under [`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc) |

## Concrete requirements

1. **Outer margins** — consistent inset from the window or dialog edge.
   Floor: **≥ 12–16 px** (CSS / Tauri), or the matching AIC Win32 dialog
   unit inset already used by sibling dialogs in the same binary. Prefer
   theme spacing tokens (`theme.spacing(…)`, shared dialog constants).
   Forbidden: ad-hoc huge stacks of empty `Box` / `mt: 8` / `mb: 8`
   spacers used only to “push content down.”

2. **No dead hero whitespace** — large empty top blocks with no content
   and no function are forbidden. A real brand header image (from
   [`branding-assets.mdc`](branding-assets.mdc) / `core-assets`) is OK
   when it is actual content. Empty spacer stacks above the first
   interactive control are not.

3. **Header proximity** — section headers and subheads sit **close** to
   the controls they label (small gap, typically ~8 px / one spacing
   unit). Put the **larger** gap **between** sections, not between a
   header and its first control.

4. **Side-by-side labels** — label-to-control horizontal gap must be
   adequate; no overlap; no label clipped at the outer margin.

5. **Control rhythm** — even vertical spacing within a group. Do not
   pack tighter than readable text or Section 508 hit-target guidance
   allows (WCAG 2.0 AA target size / spacing expectations for operator
   controls).

6. **Cross-references**
   - [`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc)
     — primary actions visible; no clipped chrome.
   - [`readable-read-only-controls.mdc`](readable-read-only-controls.mdc)
     — read-only state is not “faded / cramped.”
   - [`enterprise-compliance.mdc`](enterprise-compliance.mdc) §2 —
     Section 508 / WCAG 2.0 AA.

## Forbidden constructs

In Win32 `.rc` / dialog layout, Tauri / React operator shells, and admin
SPA layout chrome:

- Tall empty `Box` / `div` / static control whose only job is top padding
  beyond the outer-margin floor (e.g. 48–120 px of nothing above the
  first field).
- Section title with a large gap (e.g. 32–48 px) then its first control
  — invert that: tight under the header, roomy between sections.
- Controls flush against the dialog/window edge or overlapping a header
  bitmap.
- Labels truncated or painted under the left/right margin.
- Uneven “random” vertical gaps inside one field group.

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation** (Tauri / React shape — same defect appears as oversized
`cy=` / top statics in Win32 `.rc`):

```tsx
<Box sx={{ height: 72 }} /> {/* dead top zone — no content */}
<Typography variant="h6">Server connection</Typography>
<Box sx={{ height: 48 }} /> {/* huge gap under header */}
<TextField label="Server URL" … />
```

**Fix**:

```tsx
<Box sx={{ p: 2 }}> {/* outer margin ≥ 12–16 px via theme token */}
  <Typography variant="h6" sx={{ mb: 1 }}>
    Server connection
  </Typography>
  {/* ~8 px under header, then fields; larger gap only before next section */}
  <Stack spacing={1.5}>
    <TextField label="Server URL" … />
    <TextField label="Port" … />
  </Stack>
  <Box sx={{ mt: 3 }}>
    <Typography variant="h6" sx={{ mb: 1 }}>
      Diagnostics
    </Typography>
    <Stack spacing={1.5}>{/* … */}</Stack>
  </Box>
</Box>
```

Win32 parallel: collapse oversized top blank statics; place the first
`LTEXT` / group header a dialog-unit or two above its first edit /
combo; keep left/right margins aligned with sibling AIC dialogs.

## Required agent behavior

1. When generating or editing any operator GUI, apply this rule in the
   same change set — do not “fix spacing later.”
2. Prefer shared spacing constants / theme tokens over one-off pixel
   stacks.
3. Before claiming a layout fix is done, capture visual proof per
   [`essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc`](essential-ui-actions-must-be-visible.mdc)
   when the change is visual.
4. New always-apply rules under `c:\analog-pim\.cursor\rules\` must be
   mirrored to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change set
   ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

## Origin

2026-08-03 — operator hard rule: margins/spacing keep getting violated
by default; codify floors, forbid top dead zones, keep headers close to
